# Inert original-owner pin evaluation candidate

This candidate propagates closed optional prepared hooks through original owner_policy/owner_current, policy resolve/active_component/reference_values/envelope validation, scoped application/source health, and D11 document-storage/owner validation. Default callers keep original native predicates, catches and order. No route/registry/migration/main integration is installed.

OwnerReader is restricted to exact registered selected claim/resolution permits after a fresh historical scope-only permission pipeline. Original actor is server-derived and freshly loaded, never substituted into observer context. Native original owner case/document/template grants and finance-scope finance.read remain unchanged. Null owner pin returns false before User/policy/lock work. Retractions are excluded. Returned owner_authority_pin_current means only exact native original-owner policy ID match, never template selection/status/usable document authority.

The fixed reader uses scalar views and named lookup purposes. Original scalar identities, absent application, latest configuration/source states, native ANY-historical active/revoked family head and observed grant truth are explicit fixed EXISTS/NOT EXISTS/latest-order predicates attached to BOTH metadata and BYTEA transfer. Reference stored sha256/schema_ref are included, not just case/ref/version. No generic SQL replay engine or arbitrary caller SQL is installed. Final SELECT1 rechecks retained guards; it is not a substitute for pretransfer predicates. Native family tie ordering remains revision-only, not an invented PK preference; any guard mismatch is an engineering hold.

Cells use the existing policy phase ledger and fresh decode. No unguarded ORM envelope/content/bindings/paths are used on prepared path. Each scalar query/native grant query/native mutex spends an entry-shared permit. Entry caps:100 selected operations;100 identities per category,400 total typed identities,1000 scalar evaluations. Configuration candidates share the100 configuration identity cap across wrappers/operations, with exhaustive admitted latest-state scan, not early winner truncation. Existing cell100/1MiB/global and policy phase limits remain separate. These bound admitted results/calls, not SQL scan cost/planner memory/lock wait.

PreparedOwnerStop is outside every native catch family. Engineering transfer/context/shape failure poisons entry and cannot become false/INVALID. Native predicate PD/VE still follows its original boundary only when prepared state is clean. Missing latest states retain None/AttributeError semantics, missing references retain native first-vs-get behavior. Native source advisory xact lock remains at source_health entry; no lock or SQL has been executed during source tests.

Modern single dictionary references only are admitted. Native string/list legacy forms are explicitly engineering HOLD, never normalized or mislabeled false. Observer origin policy-read admission remains a narrower enclosing requirement, distinct from original-owner native grants. Unrelated owner grants are not added to runtime validation. Eight application envelope keys are preserved, including fixture_scope.

PURE tests extract only relevant source functions/classes and use fake transport. They do not import broad native validator modules, evaluate SQL, acquire advisory locks or run action constructors. Native/default-path equivalence, real storage SQL/locking, private fixtures, inherited-source semantics and application-route adoption remain UNRUN. The backup95afd305 and published payload exclude this later unfinished803 line unless separately backed up. Source review is required before this candidate is considered coherent; full803/Full108 not claimed.

## Pure acceptance follow-up (no production changes)

Nine additional tests compose the extracted actual OwnerReader with extracted actual PolicyCellBudget, the real existing PolicyLedger and real pure descriptor/codec. Only entry binding and cursor transport are fake. They cover three charged phases and validated tickets, shared dedup/fresh decode, conditional-row miss, charged decode failure, fingerprint conflict before second transfer, attempt/byte caps, pending tickets and cross-entry poison. This closes the former stand-in-Ledger test limitation, not SQL guard correctness.

Eight dynamic comparison tests execute extracted default functions from immutable pre-hook24c300a against current source with identical fake ORM/imports. Finite scenarios cover resolve success/missing/revoked/invalid/stale/origin failure/missing state, application absence/grants/bindings/fixture_scope, source lock ordering/revocation/validation/missing family head, D11 storage validator paths and runtime unrelated-owner omission. Call traces, results and exception type/messages match for these fixtures. Schema validation, real ORM and advisory operations remain stand-ins; this is finite dynamic control-flow comparison, not exhaustive default equivalence or native acceptance. The immutable Git baseline is read locally without checkout mutation/network access.
